      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-121012",
      ":question/problem": "A ball is kicked vertically into the air and reaches a height of $12$ meters. It returns to the ground, bounces, and then reaches a height of $8$ meters. The ball continues to bounce to heights that follow a geometric sequence. Assuming that the ball's motion is vertical throughout, calculate the total distance traveled by the ball from when it was first kicked and the fourth bounce. Round your answer to one decimal place.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
