      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-9922",
      ":question/problem": "A ball is dropped vertically from a height of $12$ meters. It bounces to a height of $8$ meters and continues to bounce to heights that follow a geometric sequence. Assuming that the ball's motion is vertical throughout, calculate the total distance it travels between the time it is dropped and the time it hits the ground for the fourth time. Round your answer to one decimal place.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
